- Name the person after `prev` as `leaving`: the k-th person counted
- Link `prev.next` to `leaving.next`, past the person leaving
- Start the next count from `prev.next`
hint: The person who leaves is the one right after `prev`, once `prev` has counted k − 1 people.
hint: Unlinking needs `leaving` to be named first, so that its `next` is known.
right: Count k − 1, name the k-th, unlink it, and carry on from the next person. Unlinking is O(1), so each round costs k steps.
wrong: Walk `prev` k − 1 steps, take `leaving = prev.next`, set `prev.next = leaving.next`, and the next round starts counting at `prev.next`.

